# Usage walkthrough for the VS Code REST Client; http/README.md lists the variables to export.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000/api
@supabaseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:54321
@publishableKey = {{$processEnv SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY}}
@email = {{$processEnv KB_EMAIL}}
@password = {{$processEnv KB_PASSWORD}}
@token = {{signIn.response.body.$.access_token}}

### 1. Sign in
# @name signIn
POST {{supabaseUrl}}/auth/v1/token?grant_type=password
apikey: {{publishableKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

### 2. The last 30 days in UTC: totals, byDay and byModel (chat, embedding, query_rewrite)
GET {{baseUrl}}/usage/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3. A window of your own, with days counted in a time zone (IANA names only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/usage/summary?from=2026-09-01T00:00:00Z&to=2026-10-01T00:00:00Z&timezone=Europe/Paris
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. An unknown time zone, or `to` before `from` → 422 invalid_payload
GET {{baseUrl}}/usage/summary?timezone=Mars/Olympus
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
